CORE gcc-only paths-lifo-expected-failure
no_fallback.c
--validate-goto-model
^\[main\.no-body\.__builtin_fputs\] .* no body for callee __builtin_fputs: FAILURE$
^\[main\.no-body\.__builtin_fwrite\] .* no body for callee __builtin_fwrite: FAILURE$
^\[main\.no-body\.__builtin_setjmp\] .* no body for callee __builtin_setjmp: FAILURE$
^\[vsn\.no-body\.__builtin_vsnprintf\] .* no body for callee __builtin_vsnprintf: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
pointer parameter types differ
type mismatch
not found
--
These builtins are not given the model of the C library function of the same
name without the __builtin_ prefix: __builtin_vsnprintf takes a va_list (a
struct on aarch64), __builtin_fputs and __builtin_fwrite take void * rather
than FILE * streams, and GCC's __builtin_setjmp differs from setjmp.
With --paths lifo, CBMC does not report missing function bodies, hence
paths-lifo-expected-failure.
